WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.248 --> 00:00:07.042
I had a great passion for taking
photographs of myself.

2
00:00:07.293 --> 00:00:10.503
Whenever my mother
would buy me new clothes

3
00:00:10.796 --> 00:00:13.673
I would wear them
and take photographs.

4
00:00:14.842 --> 00:00:17.385
Now I feel terrible
when I look at these.

5
00:00:18.012 --> 00:00:21.348
All I can see is how I used to look

6
00:00:21.515 --> 00:00:25.185
and how now I have
to always hide my face.

7
00:00:25.353 --> 00:00:30.857
I know I won't ever again
be as God made me

8
00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:34.110
but hopefully it will get better for me.

9
00:01:28.749 --> 00:01:30.959
<i>Patients,
register yourself at the reception.</i>

10
00:01:48.769 --> 00:01:51.271
My husband burned me.

11
00:01:51.564 --> 00:01:54.733
I was sleeping and he came inside

12
00:01:55.026 --> 00:01:56.318
and just threw acid on me.

13
00:01:56.819 --> 00:01:59.863
He just didn't want me.

14
00:02:00.573 --> 00:02:03.616
I was thirteen years old
at the time of the attack.

15
00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:08.204
My school teacher
wanted to be with me

16
00:02:08.456 --> 00:02:10.790
but I refused

17
00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:13.877
and then he threw acid on me.

18
00:02:15.004 --> 00:02:20.216
One night I was sleeping and he came
and threw acid on my shoulder.

19
00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:24.721
A year later he came back
and threw it on my face.

20
00:02:25.222 --> 00:02:29.184
All because we rejected his proposal.

21
00:02:44.061 --> 00:02:47.104
I was an innocent child.
Why did he ruin my face?

22
00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:49.398
What did I do wrong?

23
00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:18.656
Zakia, that's your name? I'm Dr. Jawad.

24
00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:24.203
I'm here working with Dr. Tariq.

25
00:06:26.998 --> 00:06:28.999
So how are you?

26
00:06:29.292 --> 00:06:30.918
I'm OK today.

27
00:06:32.045 --> 00:06:33.712
How old are you?

28
00:06:34.548 --> 00:06:35.589
Thirty-nine.

29
00:06:36.883 --> 00:06:38.801
What happened to you?

30
00:06:39.261 --> 00:06:40.511
I was attacked with acid.

31
00:06:40.679 --> 00:06:41.479
By who?

32
00:06:41.596 --> 00:06:42.930
By my husband.

33
00:06:47.936 --> 00:06:51.105
Can you take the glasses off?
Is it just your face or all over?

34
00:07:01.066 --> 00:07:04.944
Did you have any basic treatment
like a skin graft?

35
00:07:05.613 --> 00:07:07.530
They just dressed me and...

36
00:07:07.656 --> 00:07:09.991
- But no operation?
- No operation.

37
00:07:37.527 --> 00:07:39.778
My marriage went bad from the start.

38
00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:43.541
He was a drug addict and alcoholic.

39
00:07:44.668 --> 00:07:46.961
And he would take money from me

40
00:07:47.421 --> 00:07:50.423
and when I ran out of money

41
00:07:51.091 --> 00:07:52.842
he would abuse me.

42
00:07:53.051 --> 00:07:55.719
He would beat me.

43
00:07:56.430 --> 00:08:00.474
When I couldn't take it anymore I finally
went to the court to file for divorce.

44
00:08:01.876 --> 00:08:04.795
So outside the courthouse

45
00:08:05.547 --> 00:08:07.881
he confronted me.
"So you want to divorce me?"

46
00:08:08.049 --> 00:08:11.718
"I'll make a spectacle out of you
for the world to see."

47
00:08:12.053 --> 00:08:14.388
And he threw acid on me.

48
00:08:16.057 --> 00:08:18.433
He used battery acid.

49
00:08:19.102 --> 00:08:22.729
The highest quality and undiluted.

50
00:08:23.648 --> 00:08:26.775
It took one second
to ruin my life completely.

51
00:08:26.943 --> 00:08:28.819
One second.

52
00:08:31.281 --> 00:08:35.951
He thought he could just escape
and no one would find out.

53
00:08:36.452 --> 00:08:39.413
But he got caught and now he's in jail.

54
00:08:39.539 --> 00:08:42.457
And there's an ongoing case
against him.

55
00:08:53.737 --> 00:08:54.778
<i>Are you married?</i>

56
00:08:54.905 --> 00:08:55.779
Yes.

57
00:08:56.239 --> 00:08:57.079
<i>Do you have children?</i>

58
00:08:57.199 --> 00:08:58.199
No, I don't.

59
00:08:58.784 --> 00:08:59.992
<i>What's your wife's name?</i>

60
00:09:01.328 --> 00:09:03.996
I don't think it's important
to tell you that.

61
00:09:09.044 --> 00:09:10.711
<i>Did you give her a divorce?</i>

62
00:09:10.962 --> 00:09:11.837
No.

63
00:09:12.088 --> 00:09:13.380
<i>Why not?</i>

64
00:09:13.965 --> 00:09:15.841
She's mine, I've married her.

65
00:09:16.051 --> 00:09:19.804
It's a matter of my dignity.
How can I just divorce her?

66
00:09:20.764 --> 00:09:23.724
<i>Why did she want to divorce you?
What happened?</i>

67
00:09:23.892 --> 00:09:25.601
Whatever happened happened.

68
00:09:28.021 --> 00:09:30.564
I never intended to do this

69
00:09:30.774 --> 00:09:32.691
and I didn't do this.

70
00:09:35.028 --> 00:09:38.155
This is a conspiracy against me.

71
00:09:41.117 --> 00:09:42.868
<i>Some other man burned her face?</i>

72
00:09:43.161 --> 00:09:44.578
Yes.

73
00:09:44.663 --> 00:09:45.621
<i>What's his name?</i>

74
00:09:45.789 --> 00:09:47.206
I don't know his name.

75
00:09:48.124 --> 00:09:49.083
<i>But you were there.</i>

76
00:09:49.209 --> 00:09:53.587
Yes I was there but I don't know him.

77
00:09:54.464 --> 00:09:58.300
She had an affair
which no righteous husband can tolerate.

78
00:09:59.469 --> 00:10:00.269
Okay.

79
00:10:01.054 --> 00:10:02.471
This was bound to happen!

80
00:10:03.139 --> 00:10:05.724
Women are all over the place.

81
00:10:05.976 --> 00:10:08.269
Doing their "good work."

82
00:10:09.813 --> 00:10:11.063
<i>What kind of good work?</i>

83
00:10:11.982 --> 00:10:14.066
To cut the world's nose.

84
00:10:38.938 --> 00:10:41.272
Rukhsana?

85
00:10:45.319 --> 00:10:46.695
How old are you?

86
00:10:47.238 --> 00:10:48.279
Twenty-five.

87
00:10:48.881 --> 00:10:50.549
What happened to you?

88
00:10:50.842 --> 00:10:52.050
Acid attack.

89
00:10:52.218 --> 00:10:53.176
Who did it?

90
00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:58.807
My husband threw acid on me and
my sister-in-law threw gasoline on me.

91
00:10:59.183 --> 00:11:01.685
So your husband threw acid on you?

92
00:11:02.395 --> 00:11:06.606
Yes and my sister-in-law
threw gasoline on me.

93
00:11:07.859 --> 00:11:12.362
And then my mother-in-law lit a match
and set me on fire.

94
00:11:14.407 --> 00:11:15.615
And where do you live now?

95
00:11:15.783 --> 00:11:17.909
With them. I live with them.

96
00:11:18.036 --> 00:11:19.369
You still live with them?

97
00:11:19.996 --> 00:11:22.372
Yes, my kids became very sick

98
00:11:22.623 --> 00:11:26.668
and I couldn't afford
to take care of them anymore

99
00:11:26.836 --> 00:11:29.296
so I had to move back
into my husband's house

100
00:11:29.547 --> 00:11:31.923
and I had to make up with them.

101
00:12:46.032 --> 00:12:48.575
This is where they burned me alive.

102
00:12:50.161 --> 00:12:53.413
My life was destroyed in this room.

103
00:12:53.706 --> 00:12:58.501
They latched this door from outside

104
00:12:59.045 --> 00:13:01.963
so that I would suffocate to death.

105
00:13:02.173 --> 00:13:04.841
They threw acid on me, burned me alive.

106
00:13:07.345 --> 00:13:15.727
When I'm in this room I'm frightened.
I remember that incident.

107
00:13:17.688 --> 00:13:20.273
My husband has always been abusive.

108
00:13:20.483 --> 00:13:24.819
He would beat me up all the time.
Torture me.

109
00:13:29.909 --> 00:13:32.827
<i>So you have never abused your wife?</i>

110
00:13:33.079 --> 00:13:34.454
No.

111
00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:36.498
Never in these eight years of marriage.

112
00:13:36.666 --> 00:13:39.709
<i>So you never threw acid on your wife?</i>

113
00:13:39.919 --> 00:13:43.630
No. In fact nobody threw acid on her.

114
00:13:44.298 --> 00:13:46.591
She has high blood pressure
and a temper.

115
00:13:46.801 --> 00:13:49.052
When she loses her temper
she goes out of control.

116
00:13:49.428 --> 00:13:56.851
One day she lost her mind
and threw gasoline on herself.

117
00:13:57.186 --> 00:14:00.480
A candle was burning nearby.

118
00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:06.069
The gasoline accidentally fell on it
and caught fire

119
00:14:06.362 --> 00:14:09.823
and she was engulfed by the flames.

120
00:14:10.752 --> 00:14:14.327
<i>So will a married woman with two
children simply throw acid on herself?</i>

121
00:14:15.413 --> 00:14:18.915
Yes. Go visit the burn unit someday.

122
00:14:19.291 --> 00:14:20.667
You'll see

123
00:14:20.918 --> 00:14:24.587
99% of the women there

124
00:14:24.797 --> 00:14:28.717
have burned themselves alive.

125
00:14:29.885 --> 00:14:31.428
<i>What's that burn mark on your hand?</i>

126
00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:34.806
That was from...

127
00:14:35.266 --> 00:14:38.018
from when I was putting out the fire.

128
00:14:45.317 --> 00:14:47.944
Who's hiding behind the door?

129
00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:51.698
These are the new recruits.

130
00:16:02.172 --> 00:16:09.262
Older members, please tell the new people
how you went through the same thing.

131
00:16:10.973 --> 00:16:14.225
In the beginning when I first got burned
my pictures were so scary.

132
00:16:14.434 --> 00:16:18.229
My neck, everything.
I was scared to look at it.

133
00:16:18.605 --> 00:16:22.400
It took us a while to gather courage.
We used to be so scared at first.

134
00:16:22.693 --> 00:16:27.113
But now we have no such tensions.

135
00:16:29.283 --> 00:16:31.993
Zakia this is exactly
what I was telling you...

136
00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:35.121
I am not that confident.
Someday I will be.

137
00:16:36.667 --> 00:16:39.002
After meeting these women
I got a lot of courage.

138
00:16:39.011 --> 00:16:42.806
But not enough to face the world
without covering my face.

139
00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:56.161
With my face burned
I can't go to any weddings

140
00:16:56.454 --> 00:16:59.373
or funerals, or any other occasions.

141
00:18:14.951 --> 00:18:16.618
My case is ongoing.

142
00:18:16.828 --> 00:18:18.328
I have a court date tomorrow.

143
00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:21.039
I've found a lawyer.

144
00:18:26.045 --> 00:18:30.590
She is especially passionate
about women's cases.

145
00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:33.010
And she is fighting my case for free.

146
00:18:33.561 --> 00:18:36.021
I don't know how I would've fought this
without her.

147
00:18:38.116 --> 00:18:39.617
Hello Madam.

148
00:18:39.993 --> 00:18:42.286
Hello Zakia. How are you? Please sit.

149
00:18:47.742 --> 00:18:50.160
Tomorrow your court hearing begins.

150
00:18:50.829 --> 00:18:55.791
He's denied all allegations
and says he's innocent.

151
00:18:56.292 --> 00:19:00.045
"I did not throw any acid on her..."

152
00:19:00.839 --> 00:19:02.714
If not him then who threw the acid?

153
00:19:03.633 --> 00:19:06.927
Well, in order to shatter the defense

154
00:19:07.428 --> 00:19:09.805
we need to prove
that our witnesses are credible.

155
00:19:10.056 --> 00:19:14.726
I am also going to mention some verses
from the Quran on disfigurement

156
00:19:15.103 --> 00:19:17.688
in the court during our hearing.

157
00:19:18.273 --> 00:19:19.857
But it depends on the court.

158
00:19:19.983 --> 00:19:24.444
I can't say before then
what the verdict will be.

159
00:19:28.858 --> 00:19:30.525
Zakia is a very brave woman.

160
00:19:30.985 --> 00:19:36.281
Most women in our society
do not come to the courts for justice.

161
00:19:36.449 --> 00:19:42.287
Our present laws are too lenient
and most culprits are acquitted.

162
00:19:43.673 --> 00:19:48.594
It would be great if we could set
a precedent with Zakia's case.

163
00:23:37.675 --> 00:23:39.968
I suggest there should be
a death sentence.

164
00:23:40.186 --> 00:23:42.146
Ask the victims!

165
00:23:42.313 --> 00:23:45.274
Make them stand on the podium
and ask them what they want.

166
00:23:47.819 --> 00:23:52.239
The death penalty cannot be proposed
as a punishment.

167
00:23:52.532 --> 00:23:58.829
In Pakistan human rights activists
have been fighting that

168
00:23:59.122 --> 00:24:01.957
for 30 or 35 years.

169
00:24:02.083 --> 00:24:03.917
I don't think
that's going to have an impact.

170
00:24:04.252 --> 00:24:08.172
Immediately the culprit
should be taken to the town square

171
00:24:08.423 --> 00:24:10.799
and have the same thing done to him.

172
00:24:10.925 --> 00:24:12.718
If Islam permits it

173
00:24:12.927 --> 00:24:14.720
why don't we use such punishment?

174
00:24:25.940 --> 00:24:29.151
I'm very happy about
what's happening here.

175
00:24:29.778 --> 00:24:33.614
God willing this will happen.
We'll all pray for it.

176
00:24:33.782 --> 00:24:37.451
All husbands who throw acid
on their wives should be punished.

177
00:24:37.619 --> 00:24:39.411
What about the non-husbands?

178
00:24:39.621 --> 00:24:41.080
Okay even those!

179
00:24:42.624 --> 00:24:46.001
We're smiling now
because we're getting attention

180
00:24:46.211 --> 00:24:49.546
but if you look into our hearts
then you'll know what we really feel.

181
00:24:55.470 --> 00:24:59.848
I'm really nervous. How will I speak
in front of so many people?

182
00:25:00.183 --> 00:25:03.435
Come on you'll be fine.

183
00:25:06.523 --> 00:25:10.025
Even our own people
do not recognize us any more.

184
00:25:10.527 --> 00:25:13.695
This is such an injustice to us.

185
00:25:14.280 --> 00:25:17.658
Someone must stop these brutal people

186
00:25:17.909 --> 00:25:21.453
who made us into the living dead.

187
00:25:21.955 --> 00:25:25.707
Oh my fellow countrymen,
my lawmakers, my government

188
00:25:26.543 --> 00:25:29.711
your daughters seek justice from you.

189
00:25:38.829 --> 00:25:40.330
When did this happen to you?

190
00:25:40.790 --> 00:25:42.541
About two years ago.

191
00:25:42.959 --> 00:25:45.085
Although my husband was arrested
the same day

192
00:25:45.378 --> 00:25:49.807
my in-laws are wealthy
and so they all got out right away.

193
00:25:49.807 --> 00:25:50.724
So where are they now?

194
00:25:50.850 --> 00:25:52.309
They're all free.

195
00:25:53.478 --> 00:25:54.394
And what about you?

196
00:25:55.104 --> 00:25:57.856
They told me to stay quiet,
not to tell anyone.

197
00:25:58.066 --> 00:26:01.985
They told everyone that I caught fire
because an oil lamp fell on me.

198
00:26:03.363 --> 00:26:05.113
My face is ruined!

199
00:26:05.323 --> 00:26:07.157
My life is ruined!

200
00:26:07.700 --> 00:26:09.785
And nobody was punished at all.

201
00:26:10.787 --> 00:26:12.245
Where is the justice?

202
00:26:12.372 --> 00:26:14.706
Now my only request to you is that

203
00:26:14.874 --> 00:26:20.545
you do something
for helpless women like us

204
00:26:20.755 --> 00:26:24.466
so we get justice.

205
00:26:26.052 --> 00:26:31.681
If they throw acid on us, the law
should allow us to throw acid on them.

206
00:26:31.974 --> 00:26:35.852
We thought about that
but we can't permit it.

207
00:26:36.104 --> 00:26:40.941
So we have proposed a law that will
punish them with life imprisonment.

208
00:26:41.317 --> 00:26:45.529
We are trying our best to pass this law
in the assembly.

209
00:27:01.963 --> 00:27:07.217
My face is getting tighter and tighter.
It's getting worse every single day.

210
00:27:07.802 --> 00:27:10.303
It's very difficult
to even eat or drink anything.

211
00:27:11.139 --> 00:27:13.890
I can't tolerate this pain anymore.

212
00:28:20.124 --> 00:28:24.044
I'm really happy and I want to thank God

213
00:28:24.295 --> 00:28:27.714
because my wish
is about to be fulfilled.

214
00:28:32.804 --> 00:28:36.306
I hope my lips get fixed
and then my nose

215
00:28:36.599 --> 00:28:39.059
and then my eye.

216
00:28:42.688 --> 00:28:46.817
This is going to be my rebirth.

217
00:30:55.785 --> 00:30:57.369
I'm having a party.

218
00:31:01.220 --> 00:31:03.889
And if you can restore somebody's life

219
00:31:05.465 --> 00:31:09.301
I don't think I need to be bloody religious
to go where I need to go eventually.

220
00:32:16.908 --> 00:32:19.994
There is nothing in there.

221
00:32:20.921 --> 00:32:23.881
It's just illogical for it to survive
at this stage.

222
00:32:24.758 --> 00:32:25.800
I can't see anything.

223
00:32:26.009 --> 00:32:27.552
So the whole ball is shrunken so

224
00:32:27.761 --> 00:32:29.387
Dr. Ankelsaria will agree

225
00:32:29.596 --> 00:32:32.807
there's no eye to save here
and in fact the orbit

226
00:32:32.933 --> 00:32:35.726
is so badly damaged
it won't support a glass eye.

227
00:32:36.520 --> 00:32:37.728
It's too late.

228
00:32:38.480 --> 00:32:41.649
OK guys. That's unfortunate.
Let's close her up.

229
00:33:13.963 --> 00:33:17.174
By Monday or Tuesday
we'll let you go home.

230
00:33:19.302 --> 00:33:20.427
What about my nose?

231
00:33:20.970 --> 00:33:23.013
That's the next stage.

232
00:33:24.140 --> 00:33:25.683
When this is stable

233
00:33:26.351 --> 00:33:29.687
we'll have to do some
more clever things.

234
00:33:32.273 --> 00:33:35.401
We'll meet again
in the next couple months.

235
00:33:56.214 --> 00:33:58.757
They are keeping my daughter
away from me.

236
00:34:02.345 --> 00:34:04.805
My daughter lives
on the other side of this wall.

237
00:34:05.014 --> 00:34:09.935
They made this wall
so that I'd never see my daughter again.

238
00:34:11.563 --> 00:34:13.439
They won't let me be with her.

239
00:34:13.773 --> 00:34:15.733
They don't let me see her.

240
00:34:16.109 --> 00:34:19.695
They don't want me to have anything
to do with her.

241
00:34:24.868 --> 00:34:30.664
I reconciled with them for the sake
of my child but they stole her from me.

242
00:34:31.040 --> 00:34:34.918
How will I live this life
that God gave me?

243
00:34:38.047 --> 00:34:42.301
It's better to die
than to live this awful life.

244
00:34:58.735 --> 00:35:01.361
And here is the heartbeat.

245
00:35:02.831 --> 00:35:04.957
Can you see the heartbeat?

246
00:35:07.961 --> 00:35:12.673
So in fact you are pregnant
and your baby is eight weeks old.

247
00:35:15.260 --> 00:35:19.805
Didn't you take any measures
for birth control?

248
00:35:20.765 --> 00:35:24.518
Yes, I did for a while

249
00:35:24.894 --> 00:35:27.271
but then I started having problems.

250
00:35:27.606 --> 00:35:30.858
Then I left it all to God.

251
00:35:31.151 --> 00:35:35.654
Perhaps God wants to bring me joy
through this baby.

252
00:35:36.323 --> 00:35:37.448
Aren't you worried?

253
00:35:37.991 --> 00:35:44.580
Don't you realize what happened to you
could happen to your child as well?

254
00:37:31.118 --> 00:37:34.287
I am really sad
that my scheduled surgery

255
00:37:34.455 --> 00:37:36.456
won't happen.

256
00:37:40.628 --> 00:37:45.549
But my new baby
will bring happiness back to me.

257
00:37:47.218 --> 00:37:49.344
I hope I have a boy

258
00:37:50.137 --> 00:37:54.849
because a girl's future
gets risky after marriage.

259
00:37:55.059 --> 00:38:00.647
I wouldn't want my daughter
to face the same plight as me.

260
00:38:01.232 --> 00:38:05.151
In our society boys live well.

261
00:38:05.319 --> 00:38:07.612
Girls are often unhappy.

262
00:38:08.239 --> 00:38:10.574
That's why I want a baby boy.

263
00:38:32.805 --> 00:38:36.975
My husband has never seen my face
because I always wear a burqua in court.

264
00:38:37.143 --> 00:38:41.730
I always wear glasses.
He has never seen my face.

265
00:38:46.152 --> 00:38:48.111
Whenever I go to court for my hearings

266
00:38:49.280 --> 00:38:50.822
I see no remorse in his eyes.

267
00:38:52.867 --> 00:38:55.243
He stares at me
like he's going to eat me alive.

268
00:38:55.661 --> 00:38:58.913
God willing I will get justice.
I'll fight until the end.

269
00:39:00.082 --> 00:39:02.626
I'm not going to let him go.
He destroyed my life.

270
00:39:07.715 --> 00:39:11.843
Our case is strong
but it's up to the judge.

271
00:39:12.362 --> 00:39:16.198
The worst-case scenario would be...

272
00:39:16.407 --> 00:39:19.034
if he is acquitted.

273
00:39:21.988 --> 00:39:24.698
He has been threatening Zakia

274
00:39:25.366 --> 00:39:29.744
so I'm worried that if he is acquitted
he might harm Zakia.

275
00:39:43.968 --> 00:39:46.845
I thought I was going to receive
the final verdict today.

276
00:39:47.180 --> 00:39:50.599
But the date was extended again
because of his lawyer.

277
00:39:51.851 --> 00:39:54.644
His lawyer does this all the time.

278
00:39:55.396 --> 00:39:58.023
I just hope
I get another court date soon.

279
00:39:58.733 --> 00:40:00.859
It's all up to God now.

280
00:40:21.339 --> 00:40:26.551
In every corner of Pakistan
there is a victim of acid crime.

281
00:40:27.094 --> 00:40:28.678
This is terrorism!

282
00:40:29.013 --> 00:40:33.975
And the culprits often go scot-free.

283
00:40:34.560 --> 00:40:37.020
God willing today a new Pakistan

284
00:40:37.438 --> 00:40:40.899
will be born
through this acid crime legislation.

285
00:40:41.108 --> 00:40:43.860
This is a gruesome crime!

286
00:40:43.986 --> 00:40:47.405
And our courts have failed
to give the culprits

287
00:40:47.532 --> 00:40:52.118
the punishment they deserve.

288
00:40:54.080 --> 00:40:58.667
Through the Acid Crime Legislation
we want a law

289
00:40:58.835 --> 00:41:01.336
that will save the life of the woman.

290
00:41:14.400 --> 00:41:18.195
Today I would like to congratulate
all the women of Pakistan

291
00:41:18.404 --> 00:41:20.697
because today history was made.

292
00:41:20.865 --> 00:41:25.619
Our fight is not over yet.
It still continues.

293
00:41:25.912 --> 00:41:27.371
Thank you.

294
00:41:47.708 --> 00:41:51.002
Ever since I filed the charges
he's been threatening me.

295
00:41:52.129 --> 00:41:57.175
He says, "When I get out
I'll destroy your entire family."

296
00:41:58.094 --> 00:42:00.845
I can't take it anymore.

297
00:42:02.431 --> 00:42:06.643
I pray that they can keep him in jail.

298
00:42:10.314 --> 00:42:11.674
You didn't say your prayers today?

299
00:42:11.732 --> 00:42:12.532
No.

300
00:42:12.532 --> 00:42:15.576
- Why didn't you? Didn't feel like it?
- I don't know.

301
00:42:15.861 --> 00:42:18.571
- Did you get lazy?
- No that's not the case.

302
00:42:18.697 --> 00:42:19.906
Okay.

303
00:42:20.449 --> 00:42:21.741
Will you go to school tomorrow?

304
00:42:21.867 --> 00:42:24.702
I'm not sure if I will.
I don't feel like it.

305
00:42:24.870 --> 00:42:26.830
You don't feel like it? Why not?

306
00:42:26.997 --> 00:42:28.957
I'm really nervous.

307
00:42:29.083 --> 00:42:32.460
I can't take these hardships on us
anymore.

308
00:42:39.301 --> 00:42:42.679
I just want everything to be over.

309
00:42:42.888 --> 00:42:46.307
And that will finally be
a happy day for us.

310
00:42:46.809 --> 00:42:50.311
You should pray for God's will
to end all of this.

311
00:42:55.359 --> 00:42:57.277
- Tell me a joke.
- Should I tell a joke?

312
00:42:57.570 --> 00:42:59.070
Tell the one with the cat

313
00:42:59.196 --> 00:43:03.116
- the one where it changes colors...
- I don't know that one, I've forgotten it.

314
00:43:03.409 --> 00:43:05.326
Okay. Tell me one you remember...

315
00:44:48.229 --> 00:44:49.437
Greetings, Madam.

316
00:44:49.897 --> 00:44:55.819
Hello please sit.

317
00:45:04.170 --> 00:45:05.587
Zakia your verdict has come.

318
00:45:06.881 --> 00:45:08.161
Do you want to know the details?

319
00:45:08.161 --> 00:45:10.081
Yes please,
I have been waiting anxiously for it.

320
00:45:10.593 --> 00:45:13.386
It's a very detailed verdict.

321
00:45:14.013 --> 00:45:15.847
Everything has been discussed.

322
00:45:18.684 --> 00:45:21.019
And his motive is also mentioned in it.

323
00:45:21.270 --> 00:45:23.230
Yes Madam tell me the verdict.

324
00:45:25.858 --> 00:45:30.570
Under Act 7C in the 7th section...

325
00:45:32.031 --> 00:45:32.864
Yes?

326
00:45:35.409 --> 00:45:37.786
He has been given two life sentences!

327
00:45:38.371 --> 00:45:42.499
- Not one but two life sentences!
- Thanks a million to God.

328
00:45:53.144 --> 00:45:56.271
First tell me what happened
with your court case?

329
00:45:56.439 --> 00:45:59.691
He received a double life sentence.

330
00:46:03.905 --> 00:46:07.658
Sir, this is the first time ever
to punish a case under the new law.

331
00:46:07.784 --> 00:46:11.954
- You are the first case to be tried
under this law? - Yes.

332
00:46:14.666 --> 00:46:15.466
How do you feel?

333
00:46:15.667 --> 00:46:16.875
I feel great!

334
00:46:17.502 --> 00:46:19.294
It's a strong message.

335
00:46:19.671 --> 00:46:22.714
They used to think it's a joke.

336
00:46:22.840 --> 00:46:25.509
That nothing will ever happen.

337
00:46:26.386 --> 00:46:27.844
I admire your courage.

338
00:46:27.929 --> 00:46:29.262
I'm really proud of you.

339
00:46:36.688 --> 00:46:38.271
Do you remember her?

340
00:46:40.358 --> 00:46:43.527
Your face has settled well.

341
00:46:43.653 --> 00:46:46.530
I'm really pleased.

342
00:46:46.990 --> 00:46:50.617
Zakia, the last time we operated on you

343
00:46:50.952 --> 00:46:54.454
we realized that your eye
is completely damaged.

344
00:46:54.872 --> 00:46:57.791
It won't even support a glass eye.

345
00:46:58.209 --> 00:47:01.044
There's only so much I can do for you.

346
00:47:01.796 --> 00:47:05.048
We have our limitations.

347
00:47:07.635 --> 00:47:09.136
We can't be God.

348
00:47:09.387 --> 00:47:12.347
To recreate all your loss

349
00:47:12.640 --> 00:47:15.934
such as your eyebrows,
eyelashes and eyelids

350
00:47:16.269 --> 00:47:20.272
for that I've got a top guy from Dubai

351
00:47:20.565 --> 00:47:23.191
who will make a prosthesis for you.

352
00:47:23.693 --> 00:47:29.031
But you'll have to wear
that prosthesis externally.

353
00:47:30.992 --> 00:47:32.826
So that's my plan? All right?

354
00:48:33.796 --> 00:48:35.380
Brilliant.

355
00:48:37.383 --> 00:48:40.385
First I thank God

356
00:48:40.803 --> 00:48:43.305
then I thank you.

357
00:48:46.225 --> 00:48:49.436
Come meet your mother.

358
00:48:51.230 --> 00:48:52.355
How do I look?

359
00:48:52.481 --> 00:48:53.606
You look fantastic.

360
00:48:53.733 --> 00:48:54.899
She really looks fantastic.

361
00:48:56.110 --> 00:48:57.944
You've got your old mom back?

362
00:48:58.446 --> 00:49:00.530
She was lost for awhile wasn't she?

363
00:49:17.832 --> 00:49:19.165
How are you?

364
00:49:19.625 --> 00:49:20.500
Fine.

365
00:49:20.551 --> 00:49:22.886
Congratulations on your boy.

366
00:49:25.806 --> 00:49:27.140
What name have you given him?

367
00:49:27.850 --> 00:49:29.309
Mohammad.

368
00:49:31.020 --> 00:49:36.483
And I hope that he studies hard
and becomes a doctor like you.

369
00:49:36.734 --> 00:49:38.610
And not like his father.

370
00:49:43.032 --> 00:49:44.574
God willing.

371
00:49:44.742 --> 00:49:46.576
I will fulfill my promise to you.

372
00:49:47.411 --> 00:49:52.582
But we must wait for
about six months or so.

373
00:49:53.042 --> 00:49:57.045
Then we'll do our surgery on you.

374
00:50:34.709 --> 00:50:35.509
You look beautiful.

375
00:50:35.876 --> 00:50:36.876
Really?

376
00:50:38.504 --> 00:50:40.004
Today is the first day

377
00:50:40.172 --> 00:50:43.299
since the acid attack that I've left
my house without my veil.

378
00:50:43.426 --> 00:50:46.344
Without my burqua,
without my sunglasses.

379
00:50:51.183 --> 00:50:53.101
I feel really good.

380
00:50:54.770 --> 00:50:57.731
I have changed a lot
since my acid attack.

381
00:50:59.817 --> 00:51:03.236
And hopefully some of these things
will still get worked out.

382
00:51:04.864 --> 00:51:06.906
I am ready to begin my new life.

383
00:51:07.533 --> 00:51:10.410
And God willing tomorrow
seems much better than today.
